  saveReview,              // (week, data) => void
  listReviews,             // () => array

  // ── Onboarding ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  getOnboarding,           // (agentId) => checklist|null
  saveOnboarding,          // (agentId, data) => void

  // ── Pending Approvals ───────────────────────────────────────
  loadApprovals,           // () => array
  saveApproval,            // (approval) => void
  removeApproval,          // (key) => void

  // ── Chat History ────────────────────────────────────────────
  loadChatHistory,         // () => array of { id, title, updatedAt, messageCount }
  getChatSession,          // (id) => { id, title, messages, ... }
  saveChatSession,         // ({ id, title, messages }) => { id }
  deleteChatSession,       // (id) => void

  // ── Project Conversations ───────────────────────────────────
  loadProjectConversations,   // (projectId) => array (lightweight)
  getProjectConversation,     // (projectId, id) => full conversation
  createProjectConversation,  // (projectId, { title, agentName }) => convo
  deleteProjectConversation,  // (projectId, id) => void
  addConversationMessage,     // (conversationId, { role, content }) => message

  // ── Singleton Configs ───────────────────────────────────────
  loadConfig,              // () => { projectDirs, backup, ... }
  saveConfig,              // (data) => void
  loadGoals,               // () => { mission, projectGoals, agentGoals }
  saveGoals,               // (data) => void
  loadModelRouting,        // () => { rules, costs }
  saveModelRouting,        // (data) => void
  loadAgentLearning,       // () => { agents, taskTypes, routing }
  saveAgentLearning,       // (data) => void
  loadClaims,              // () => { [taskId]: claim }
  saveClaims,              // (data) => void
  loadRecommendations,     // () => object
  saveRecommendations,     // (data) => void
  loadAntipatternSigs,     // () => array
  saveAntipatternSigs,     // (data) => void
  loadSkillIndex,          // () => object
  saveSkillIndex,          // (data) => void

  // ── Migration ───────────────────────────────────────────────
  runMigrations,           // (db) => void (called internally by getDb)
  importFromJson,          // () => { imported, errors }
};
```

**Key design decisions for the API:**

1. **`insertAgentRun` replaces the write-queue pattern.** SQLite WAL mode handles concurrent writes natively. No queue needed.

2. **`queryAgentRuns` replaces the load-all-then-filter pattern** in `/api/analytics/runs`. The SQL `WHERE` clause does the filtering, and `LIMIT/OFFSET` handles pagination -- turning an O(n) memory operation into an O(log n) index lookup.

3. **`getAgentRunsSummary` replaces the in-memory aggregation** loop in `/api/analytics/summary` with a single SQL `GROUP BY` query.

4. **Chat messages are normalized** into a separate table, so `loadChatHistory` can return `messageCount` via `COUNT(*)` instead of loading every message into memory.

5. **Singleton tables** use `INSERT OR REPLACE` with `id = 1` constraint, so `loadConfig()` is just `SELECT data FROM config WHERE id = 1` and `saveConfig()` is `INSERT OR REPLACE INTO config (id, data) VALUES (1, ?)`.

---

### 5. Index Strategy Rationale

| Index | Table | Why |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `idx_agent_runs_filter(agentName, status, timestamp)` | agent_runs | Covers the `/api/analytics/runs` query with all 3 filter params in one index scan |
| `idx_agent_runs_timestamp(timestamp DESC)` | agent_runs | `loadRecentAgentRuns(hours)` needs fast time-range scan |
| `idx_witness_log_t(t DESC)` | witness_log | Witness sweep reads last N days; descending for newest-first |
| `idx_witness_log_agent(agent)` | witness_log | `getWitnessLog({ agent })` filter |
| `idx_daily_scores_agent_date(agent, date)` UNIQUE | daily_scores | Prevents duplicate daily score per agent; fast lookup for trend queries |
| `idx_memory_audit_path(path)` | memory_audit_log | `/api/memory/history/file/:filePath` endpoint |
| `idx_chat_messages_session(sessionId)` | chat_messages | Loading messages for a single session |
| `idx_claims_status(status)` | claims | The stale-claim cleanup runs every 5 min filtering by status |
| `idx_agents_department(department)` | agents | `findAgentsByDepartment()` |

**No indexes on:** singleton tables (only 1 row), orchestrations (scanned by PK or full-table, max 100 rows), webhooks (max 10 rows), reviews (max 52/year).

